          "name": "owner",
          "docs": [
            "Seed material for the Pot, the destination for its rent, and the authorization for the",
            "close — all three, which is why it signs."
          ],
          "writable": true,
          "signer": true
        },
        {
          "name": "engine_program",
          "docs": [
            "constraints there can name it — Anchor evaluates fields in declaration order."
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "pot",
          "docs": [
            "this instruction's to enforce rather than the CPI's.",
            "",
            "**It must exist.** A derivation naming no live account would otherwise reach `close_account`",
            "and be refused there; checked here so a mistyped salt says so instead of reporting a rent",
            "reclaim that did not happen.",
            "",
            "**The engine must own it.** Note the two senses of \"owner\" meeting on one line below:",
            "`pot.owner` is Solana's — the PROGRAM that may mutate the account — while the `owner` field",
            "above is this kitchen's, the user who may act on the Pot. They are never the same value.",
            "The name follows the EVM Kitchen's, where a Pot's `owner` is likewise the user.",
            "",
            "Leaving the ownership check to the runtime is not enough: the runtime only",
            "refuses a program that *attempts* the debit, so pointing `engine_program` at anything that",
            "accepts arbitrary data and returns `Ok` would make the CPI succeed, this handler return",
            "`Ok`, and the caller believe the Pot was closed while it sits untouched with its rent. This",
            "instruction is the one making the promise, so it is the one that checks."
          ],
          "writable": true,
          "pda": {
            "seeds": [
              {
