        {
          "name": "engine_program",
          "docs": [
            "deliberately validates nothing about it.",
            "",
            "An address with no program behind it is accepted and produces an unusable Pot: nothing can",
            "write it (only an owner may mutate account data) and nothing can close it (only an owner may",
            "debit its lamports), so its rent is stranded and `space` is already fixed forever. An",
            "`executable` constraint would catch that, and was deliberately not added — the loss is one",
            "Pot's rent, and the EVM side takes the same posture for the same reason. Choosing the wrong",
            "interpreter is the caller's business either way."
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "pot",
          "docs": [
            "engine owns the bytes, and their layout is the compiled program's business, not ours.",
            "Anchor's `init` fails loudly if the account already exists, which is the \"fails cleanly on a",
            "Pot that exists\" half of the acceptance criteria; `create_pot` is not idempotent.",
            "",
            "The range sits on the account whose size it decides. Anchor runs every field's",
            "deserialization — `init` included — before any `constraint`, so no position in this struct",
            "makes it a precondition of the allocation; a rejected `space` unwinds the whole instruction",
            "instead, which is what keeps a useless Pot from ever reaching the chain. The upper half is a",
            "floor for `MAX_POT_LEN` rather than the live check: at today's value it equals the runtime's",
            "own per-instruction allocation ceiling, which refuses anything larger first."
          ],
          "writable": true,
          "pda": {
            "seeds": [
              {
                "kind": "const",
                "value": [
                  112,
                  111,
                  116
